From 9ac7a64c887caa195bda0860fb37cd3fbd11b845 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shorinkiwata <fcl709@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:43:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: Show systray icons as StatusNotifierItems.

Panels on Wayland compositors, and KDE and GNOME, only show tray icons
through the StatusNotifierItem D-Bus protocol, not the XEmbed system tray.
Applications that hide their window to the tray then cannot be brought
back.

Every icon gets its own connection and well-known name. Clicks reported
by the host are turned into the mouse messages a docked icon gets, and
balloons are shown as desktop notifications. Without a
StatusNotifierWatcher on the session bus the icons are docked as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
